# Data conversion between bit and gibibyte

Verifies direct data conversion between bit and gibibyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1b to 0.0000GiB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5b yields 0.0000GiB; backward, converting 1GiB to 8589934592b preserves the integer representation across the integer coarser-to-finer scale, while 1.5GiB yields 12884901888.0b. Tiny magnitudes round to four fractional digits.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1b
print(forward_whole->to(GiB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5b
print(forward_fractional->to(GiB))
backward_whole: int = 1GiB
print(backward_whole->to(b))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5GiB
print(backward_fractional->to(b))

<<< stdout
0.0000GiB
0.0000GiB
8589934592b
12884901888.0b

<<< stderr
